  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xE9;ponse d&apos;urgence int&#xE9;gr&#xE9;e pour soulager les besoins vitaux imm&#xE9;diats des populations les plus vuln&#xE9;rables, touch&#xE9;es par les inondations en &#xC9;quateur, &#xE0; Kinshasa et dans la Tshopo.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide emergency assistance to the most vulnerable populations affected by flooding in Ecuador, Kinshasa, and Tshopo. This CERF project focuses on the WASH, Health and child protection sectors, and aims to contribute to: improving access to WASH services through the disinfection and rehabilitation of water points; improving access to primary health care through the light rehabilitation of health structures affected, and strengthened surveillance systems; and strengthening child protection services in affected areas, among others. Through these activities, this project aims to lessen the impact of flooding on affected populations. The project provides life-saving assistance to over 137,000 people, including 22,866 women, 94,734 children, and including 19,831 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
